WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.980
0

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.730
on

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.120
Robotic snakes sound like the stuff of
nightmares.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.900
But their limbless movements make them
good candidates for exploring land, sea

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.640
and air.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.520
On a recent expedition Egypt. a robotics
team ran into trouble.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.000
Their robo snake couldn't make its way
up sandy inclines.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.050
"We're often as is interested in failures

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.800
of locomotive models as we are
success because the failures help us

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.310
understand some of the principles."

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.810
Meanwhile... a  physics team in Georgia was working out the biomechanics of snakes

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:40.770
on tilted sandy soils. "We thought to
yourself what's a very cool animal

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.850
that no one is looked at?" As it turned
out

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:50.120
robots aren't the only ones to have problems
with the sand. But one snake had no issues 

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.790
ascending the steepest slopes

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:56.170
the Sidewinder rattlesnake. When
sidewinders sidewind

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.980
they're actually sending two waves down
their body: one in the horizontal plane

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.729
and one in the vertical plane. Where
these waves meet

00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:09.150
determines which part of their bodies
move ahead in which stays stuck to the soil.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.240
Their secret to tackling slopes? Increasing the proportion of their

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.799
bodies in contact with the sand 

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:22.799
as the slope got steeper. It's harder
than it sounds.

00:01:24.829 --> 00:01:25.840
After teaming up,

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.289
the researchers use what they learned from
the Sidewinders to improve the robot

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:29.859
snake.

00:01:29.859 --> 00:01:34.179
Because the snakebot showed improvement
it meant that their understanding of

00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:35.689
sidewinding mechanics was accurate

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:38.719
and now it has the skills to slither up

00:01:38.719 --> 00:01:42.170
all the dunes in Egypt. 

